      "text": "To find the product of the two numbers, let's denote the two numbers as \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). Given that the least common multiple (LCM) of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is 36 and that their greatest common divisor (GCD) is 6, we can use the relationship between the LCM and GCD of two numbers, which is:\n\n\\[ \\text{LCM}(a, b) \\times \\text{GCD}(a, b) = a \\times b \\]\n\nSubstituting the given values into this equation, we have:\n\n\\[ 36 \\times 6 = a \\times b \\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[ a \\times b = 36 \\times 6 = 216 \\]\n\nThus, the product of the two numbers is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{216}\n\\]",
